        "math_academy_id": "q-1921",
        "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)={2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}\u2061x.$",
        "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}\u2061x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20612+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u206110} \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\text{\u00a0}\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
